<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        AMENDED 2026-08-24 - THREE VALUES ADDED TO THE MASTER SET: Approved, Prepare, Review.

        Approved WAS A DIRECT ORG EDIT, MADE OUTSIDE THIS REPO, AND THIS CHANGE IS A CATCH-UP,
        NOT A NEW DECISION. Setup already carried Approved on Disposition_NDA before this file was
        touched (confirmed via the UI API picklist-values endpoint, the only channel that reports
        record-type-scoped values correctly here - see RecordType retrieve note below). This
        change brings the repo level with the org for that one value, then adds two more
        (Prepare, Review) on top, on the user's explicit instruction.

        Prepare and Review are NEW, DISPOSITION_NDA ONLY. They do not exist on Acquisition_NDA and
        must not be added there - the acquisition path is explicitly out of bounds for this
        change. Master set is still a UNION, now of two record-type sets that no longer overlap in
        size: Acquisition_NDA keeps exactly four values (Pending, Received, Signed, Sent, reordered
        2026-08-16 - see that RecordType file's own comment for why Sent is now terminal there).
        Disposition_NDA grows from four to seven: Not Sent, Approved, Sent, Signed, Declined (as
        measured live in org) plus Prepare and Review, REORDERED to
        Prepare -> Review -> Approved -> Not Sent -> Sent -> Signed -> Declined - the pre-send
        lifecycle the user described, where Approved now sits BEFORE Not Sent rather than after
        it. This is a deliberate reorder of Approved's position relative to Not Sent, not merely
        an addition; anywhere the OLD order (Not Sent before Approved) was assumed - e.g. a report
        column expecting ascending picklist order, or a components sort keyed off value order -
        should be checked. See objects/NDA__c/recordTypes/Disposition_NDA.recordType-meta.xml for
        the record-type-scoped ordering.

        MASTER (GLOBAL) VALUE SET ORDER: the pre-existing six values (Pending, Not Sent, Sent,
        Received, Signed, Declined) keep their RELATIVE order unchanged; Prepare, Review and
        Approved are inserted as a block immediately before Not Sent, matching where they sit in
        the disposition lifecycle. This is a minimal-disruption insertion, not a full reorder to
        match either record type's own sequence - the master list is a union and is never rendered
        directly once a record type is in play, since every record type here enumerates its own
        picklistValues order (see both RecordType files' own "EVERY PICKLIST ON THE OBJECT IS
        ENUMERATED" comments).

        DEFAULT VALUE NOT CHANGED. Master default stays Pending (Acquisition_NDA's entry state).
        ⚠ THE REST OF THIS PARAGRAPH IS SUPERSEDED - see the 2026-08-25 amendment at the foot of
        this comment. Kept verbatim because it names the follow-up decision the user has since
        made, and because "master default stays Pending" (the sentence above) is still true.
        RETRACTED, verbatim: "Disposition_NDA's own default stays Not Sent, NOT Prepare - this was
        a deliberate choice to avoid silently changing new-record behavior for the disposition
        path; the task adding Prepare/Review was about picklist ORDER and CONTENT, not about moving
        the record-type default earlier. If Prepare should become the default entry state for a new
        Disposition NDA, that is a follow-up decision for the user, not inferred here."

        RESTRICTED PICKLIST, DML-ENFORCED (measured, not assumed - see
        recordTypes/Acquisition_NDA.recordType-meta.xml's 2026-08-20 correction). Deploy order is
        therefore load-bearing: this field (the superset) must deploy before or with the
        RecordType files that narrow it, never after a Disposition_NDA file that already
        references a value this file doesn't yet carry.

        ROLLUP SAFETY CHECKED 2026-08-24 (Task 3 of this change) - flows/NDA_Signed_Rollup's
        Is_Row_Signed decision has exactly two named outcomes, Signed and Declined; every other
        value, INCLUDING the three added here, falls through its default connector
        ("Outstanding - count the total only") into Count_Row, which increments NDA_Count__c but
        NOT Signed_NDA_Count__c. That is the correct, fail-CLOSED behavior for Prepare/Review/
        Approved: each counts as an outstanding party toward the total, so
        All_NDAs_Signed_Before_Progression's BLANKVALUE(Signed_NDA_Count__c,0) &lt;
        BLANKVALUE(NDA_Count__c,0) clause keeps blocking every forward stage until the party
        actually reaches Signed. NO FLOW CHANGE WAS MADE OR IS NEEDED for this reason - the
        rollup's default branch already treats "anything that isn't Signed or Declined" as
        outstanding, and that default already covers the three new values without being told
        their names.

        =====================================================================
        AMENDED 2026-08-25 - 'Not Sent' IS NOW ON NO RECORD TYPE, AND Disposition_NDA HAS NO
        DEFAULT. THIS FIELD FILE ITSELF IS UNCHANGED BELOW THE COMMENT - THE VALUE STAYS ACTIVE ON
        THE MASTER SET.
        =====================================================================

        The user removed 'Not Sent' from Disposition_NDA in Setup and cleared that record type's
        default; the repo caught up in
        objects/NDA__c/recordTypes/Disposition_NDA.recordType-meta.xml, whose own 2026-08-25
        amendment carries the measured evidence. Disposition_NDA now exposes SIX values:
        Prepare -> Review -> Approved -> Sent -> Signed, plus Declined.
        ⚠ SUPERSEDED HOURS LATER THE SAME DAY - IT IS FIVE VALUES, NOT SIX. See the second
        2026-08-25 amendment below; 'Review' left the record type too. Kept verbatim because it
        records what was true when 'Not Sent' was removed.

        🔴 'Not Sent' IS DELIBERATELY LEFT ACTIVE IN THE <valueSet> BELOW even though Acquisition_
        NDA already restricted it out, which makes it reachable from NO record type. Deactivating
        it would break the rows that already carry it - and there are such rows in usman-dpeg. It
        is now a LEGACY-READ-ONLY value: readable, renderable, formula-mappable, but refused on any
        new write because this value set is `restricted` and DML enforces the record-type subset
        (measured; see recordTypes/Acquisition_NDA.recordType-meta.xml's 2026-08-20 correction).
        Anyone tempted to prune it, or to prune the consumers that still name it
        (Tracking_Status__c's CASE, RecordStageAdvanceService's 'Not Sent' => 'Sent' hop,
        dispositionDealSummary's NDA_TONE), is pruning the ONLY thing keeping those rows working.

        =====================================================================
        AMENDED 2026-08-25, LATER THE SAME DAY - 'Review' IS ALSO NOW ON NO RECORD TYPE. THIS FIELD
        FILE'S <valueSet> IS AGAIN UNCHANGED - THE VALUE STAYS ACTIVE ON THE MASTER SET.
        =====================================================================

        The user removed 'Review' from Disposition_NDA in Setup, hours after this file added it.
        The repo caught up in recordTypes/Disposition_NDA.recordType-meta.xml, whose second
        2026-08-25 amendment carries the measured evidence. Disposition_NDA now exposes FIVE
        values: Prepare -> Approved -> Sent -> Signed, plus Declined.

        SO OF THE THREE VALUES THIS FILE ADDED ON 2026-08-24, ONE (Review) SURVIVED ON A RECORD
        TYPE FOR ABOUT A DAY. It is left ACTIVE below for the same mechanical reason 'Not Sent' is
        - deactivating a value is the change that breaks rows - but the justification is NOT the
        same and should not be quoted as such: a live aggregate on 2026-08-25 found ZERO NDA rows
        at 'Review' on either record type (and, contrary to the paragraph above, zero at
        'Not Sent' either).

        🔴 'Review' IS THEREFORE AN ORPHAN ON THIS VALUE SET: on no record type, on no row, and
        UNWRITABLE because this set is RESTRICTED and DML enforces the record-type subset. It is
        REPORTED AS SUCH RATHER THAN DEACTIVATED HERE - deactivating it is a separate decision for
        the user, and 'Not Sent' is in exactly the same state and would deserve the same treatment
        at the same time.

        ⚠ ITS CONSUMERS WERE PRUNED, WHICH IS WHERE THIS DIFFERS FROM 'Not Sent'. The
        'Prepare' => 'Review' and 'Review' => 'Approved' hops are gone from
        RecordStageAdvanceService (they were a LIVE DEFECT - the Advance quick action threw
        "bad value for restricted picklist field: Review" on the first click of every new
        disposition NDA), the 'Review' branch is gone from Tracking_Status__c's CASE, and the
        Review step is gone from NDA_Path_Disposition. Do not restore any of them.

        ⚠ WHERE A NEW DISPOSITION NDA NOW STARTS. With no record-type default, a UI-created NDA
        leaves Status__c BLANK. Automation does not: DispositionStageEntryService's
        DISPOSITION_NDA_INITIAL_STATUS moved 'Not Sent' -> 'Prepare' in this same change, as did
        TestDataFactory's disposition seed. THAT CONSTANT IS NOW THE ONLY DECLARATION OF THE ENTRY
        STATE ANYWHERE - there is no <default>true</default> left on the record type to keep it in
        step with, so a future reorder of the lifecycle must edit the constant explicitly.
    -->
    <fullName>Status__c</fullName>
    <description>Lifecycle state of the NDA. THE MASTER SET IS THE UNION OF TWO RECORD-TYPE SETS AND NO SINGLE RECORD TYPE SEES ALL VALUES. Acquisition_NDA exposes Pending, Received, Signed, Sent (D14.1, reordered 2026-08-16). Disposition_NDA exposes Prepare, Approved, Sent, Signed, Declined (2026-08-25 - &apos;Not Sent&apos; and &apos;Review&apos; both removed from that type; both stay ACTIVE here and are now on NO record type - see XML comment). Sent and Signed are SHARED, so this field alone does NOT identify the record type - use Disposition__c or RecordTypeId for that. Read by NDA_Signed_Status_Sync (before-save, derives NDA_Signed__c) and NDA_Signed_Rollup (after-save, counts Signed rows onto the parent Disposition).</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Pick the state this NDA is in. The choices differ by record type: an acquisition NDA runs Pending, Received, Signed, Sent; a disposition NDA runs Prepare, Approved, Sent, Signed, and Declined if the counterparty refuses.</inlineHelpText>
